Grammar

Rule 0     S' -> command
Rule 1     command -> action COORDINATE
Rule 2     action -> ATACAR
Rule 3     action -> DEFENDER

Terminals, with rules where they appear

ATACAR               : 2
COORDINATE           : 1
DEFENDER             : 3
error                : 

Nonterminals, with rules where they appear

action               : 1
command              : 0

Parsing method: LALR

state 0

    (0) S' -> . command
    (1) command -> . action COORDINATE
    (2) action -> . ATACAR
    (3) action -> . DEFENDER

    ATACAR          shift and go to state 3
    DEFENDER        shift and go to state 4

    command                        shift and go to state 1
    action                         shift and go to state 2

state 1

    (0) S' -> command .



state 2

    (1) command -> action . COORDINATE

    COORDINATE      shift and go to state 5


state 3

    (2) action -> ATACAR .

    COORDINATE      reduce using rule 2 (action -> ATACAR .)


state 4

    (3) action -> DEFENDER .

    COORDINATE      reduce using rule 3 (action -> DEFENDER .)


state 5

    (1) command -> action COORDINATE .

    $end            reduce using rule 1 (command -> action COORDINATE .)

